From 350d80c0a55e5fb85bdc297a77210138e98e9302 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:52:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 39/42] Finder: Google Drive notices revoked sign-ins

A running rclone mount doesn't exit when Google revokes its token; it
only logs failed requests. Finder now catches this three ways:

- it follows the service's log;
- once a minute, it asks Google for the quota through rclone's rc
  (operations/about, which needs --rc-no-auth; the socket sits in the
  0700 runtime dir);
- it reads the log when the service fails at startup.

Once signed out, Finder stops the service and stays signed out until
the user signs in again, instead of flipping back to Ready while the
mount comes down. The unit now has a start limit, so a dead token
can't make it retry forever, and sign-in/start reset that limit before
restarting, in order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
